# Arduino build
inputs/firmware/opta/build/
scanmania.db*

# Calibration artefacts. tools/capture.py writes a timestamped backup and a
# .new temp file beside beams.json; deploy.sh does `git add config`, so these
# were being committed and pushed on every deploy, and a kill mid-write left a
# stray .new behind that the next deploy swept into the repo.
config/*.bak
config/*.json.*.bak
config/*.json.new
config/*.tmp

# Audio. The soundtrack is scp'd to the box, not carried in git: a single
# ambient bed is 14 MB and the repo is cloned and pulled far more often than
# the music changes. sounds/README.md documents the layout and the ffmpeg
# recipe for cutting a seamless loop; tools/gen_placeholder_sounds.py writes
# stand-in tones so a fresh checkout still has something to play.
# deploy.sh pulls, and git leaves ignored files alone, so the real audio
# survives every deploy untouched.
sounds/*.wav
sounds/*.mp3
sounds/*.ogg
sounds/*.flac

# The sendable update kit is built from tools/update-kit/ on demand:
#   cd tools && zip -r scanmania-update.zip update-kit
# The folder is tracked; the zip is not — a binary that regenerates from
# tracked files does not belong in the history.
tools/scanmania-update.zip
